data.content:
**No Thread.Abort migration is needed here.**

Your code only uses `Thread.Start()`, `Thread.Join()`, and `Thread.Sleep()` — none of which involve `Thread.Abort`, `ThreadAbortException`, `Thread.ResetAbort`, or `Thread.Interrupt`. These APIs work identically in .NET 8 and require no changes.

This code will compile and run correctly as-is on `net8.0`.

---

**Optional modernization** (unrelated to Thread.Abort migration):

You could simplify with `Parallel.ForEach` or `Task.WhenAll`:

```csharp
public class SimpleWorker
{
    public void RunBatch(List<WorkItem> items)
    {
        Parallel.ForEach(items, item => Process(item));
    }

    private void Process(WorkItem item)
    {
        Thread.Sleep(100);
        item.Result = ComputeResult(item.Input);
    }
}
```

This is purely a modernization choice — not a requirement for the migration to succeed.
